     3	## What is proven
     4	
     5	Under the supplied `MPY` semantics, for every finite modeled string whose code
     6	sequence contains only ASCII lowercase letters (`97`–`122`) and ASCII spaces
     7	(`32`), loading `solution.mpy`'s exact `histogram` function body and calling it
     8	returns `histogramResult(CS)`.
     9	
    10	`histogramResult(CS)` is a dictionary whose keys are exactly the distinct
    11	non-space letters attaining the greatest occurrence count in `CS`, and whose
    12	value at each key is that count. The empty or all-space input returns the empty
    13	dictionary. Dictionary key order is first-occurrence order, although the prompt
    14	does not observe order.
    15	
    16	This is a K reachability proof of partial correctness. It does not separately
    17	claim termination.
